  toc={toc}
  publishDate="2026-03-28"
  updateDate="2026-09-11"
>

<p>No free tool covers a complete website audit. Build a small toolkit: Search Console for Google's observed search data, a crawler for site-wide URL evidence, page tools for performance and accessibility, and focused security checks. Keep each result attached to the URL, date and test conditions.</p>

<h2 id="google-search-console">Google Search Console</h2>

<p><a href="https://search.google.com/search-console/about" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Search Console</a> reports Google Search performance, indexing, crawling and enhancement data for verified properties. Use it to inspect Google's observed state and submitted sitemaps. It does not replace a full site crawl, and its reports can aggregate, filter or delay data.</p>

<h2 id="google-lighthouse">Google Lighthouse</h2>

<p><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/lighthouse/overview/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lighthouse</a> audits one page in a lab environment for performance, accessibility, SEO and other quality checks. Run repeat tests under comparable conditions and open the evidence behind each failed audit. See our <a href="/website-audit-tools/lighthouse/">Lighthouse interpretation guide</a>.</p>

<h2 id="google-pagespeed-insights">Google PageSpeed Insights</h2>

<p><a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev/" rel="noopener noreferrer">PageSpeed Insights</a> combines a Lighthouse lab run with Chrome User Experience Report field data when eligible data exists. Use field LCP, INP and CLS to understand real-user experience, and lab diagnostics to investigate. A URL may have no field data when the CrUX dataset lacks sufficient coverage.</p>

<h2 id="screaming-frog-free-version">Screaming Frog Free Version</h2>

<p><a href="https://www.screamingfrog.co.uk/seo-spider/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Screaming Frog SEO Spider</a> is a desktop crawler. Its free version crawls up to 500 URLs in one crawl and exports common link, response, directive and on-page fields. Saving crawls, JavaScript rendering, custom extraction, API integrations and scheduling require the paid version.</p>

<h2 id="ahrefs-webmaster-tools">Ahrefs Free</h2>

<p><a href="https://ahrefs.com/webmaster-tools" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ahrefs Webmaster Tools is now Ahrefs Free</a>. It provides Site Audit and selected Site Explorer access for verified sites. Ahrefs listed 5,000 Site Audit crawl credits per verified project per month on 11 September 2026; check the current allowance before planning recurring crawls.</p>

<h2 id="wave-accessibility-checker">WAVE Accessibility Checker</h2>

<p><a href="https://wave.webaim.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">WAVE by WebAIM</a> adds visual feedback about accessibility conditions to a page. Use it to locate automatable issues, then test keyboard access, focus, zoom, content meaning and assistive-technology output manually. Automated results do not establish WCAG conformance.</p>

<h2 id="ssl-labs">Qualys SSL Labs</h2>

<p><a href="https://www.ssllabs.com/ssltest/" rel="noopener noreferrer">SSL Labs Server Test</a> examines the public TLS endpoint and certificate configuration. It does not inspect application code, authentication or every page-level security condition. Obtain permission before testing infrastructure you do not own.</p>

<h2 id="security-headers">Security Headers</h2>

<p><a href="https://securityheaders.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Security Headers</a> reports selected HTTP response headers for a requested URL. Review the actual response across representative page types; one high-level grade is not a security audit, and a strict policy must be tested against required site behaviour.</p>

<h2 id="gtmetrix">GTmetrix</h2>

<p><a href="https://gtmetrix.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">GTmetrix</a> provides page performance tests with report and waterfall views. Record location, device, connection and test time when comparing runs. Free-account limits and test locations can change, so use the current product page rather than a stored allowance.</p>

<h2 id="webpagetest">WebPageTest</h2>

<p><a href="https://www.webpagetest.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">WebPageTest</a> provides configurable browser tests, waterfalls and visual loading evidence. Its <a href="https://github.com/catchpoint/WebPageTest.docs/blob/main/src/webpagetest-faqs.md">official documentation</a> explains browser, location and test-run options. Use it to diagnose request and rendering sequences. Choose a repeatable location, device and connection profile, and keep synthetic results separate from real-user field data.</p>

<p>For the next step, map each confirmed finding into the <a href="/website-audit-checklist/">website audit checklist</a> and retain the source report. <small>Access and product facts checked against official tool pages on 11 September 2026.</small></p>

</ContentLayout>
